Apple's logo for its upcoming September 9 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/26/apple-iphone-event-2026/">"Surprise and shine" event</a> hints at two rumored iPhone 18 Pro features, including new color options and a new camera system.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/Apple-Surprise-Shine.jpeg" alt="" width="2048" height="1152" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1061343" /><br/>
Apple fans often like to read into Apple's event invite graphics for clues about unreleased products, and this year <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman is also taking part in the fun on <a href="https://x.com/markgurman/status/2092648063395401930?s=20">Twitter (X)</a>.<br/>
<br/>
First, Gurman says he sees the shining light behind Apple's logo as a nod to the "mechanical aperture on the iPhone 18 Pro Max." <br/>
<br/>
<em>MacRumors</em> has been reporting since 2024 that Apple could introduce a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/10/27/iphone-18-pro-variable-aperture-camera/">variable aperture camera</a> on the iPhone 18 Pro models – a first for any iPhone. However, a recent rumor out of China suggests the feature could be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/18/iphone-18-pro-max-camera-upgrade-exclusive/">exclusive to the larger Pro Max model</a>.<br/>
<br/>
With a variable lens, the iPhone 18 Pro Max could allow users to manually shift the aperture, similar to on a DSLR camera. It could mean more control over depth of field and bright light, enabling sharper focus on subjects. That all depends on how Apple implements the feature, of course. It may be more automated than that.<br/>
<br/>
Second, Gurman links the sky blue color of the event invite to a "possible new iPhone 18 Pro color." According to <em>Macworld</em>, Apple will likely introduce the device in Light Blue, alongside <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/22/iphone-18-pro-foldable-iphone-rumored-colors/">Dark Cherry</a> (the new headline color), Dark Gray, and Silver.<br/>
